<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:04:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel's Arab list backs Eisenkot as Netanyahu loses ultra-Orthodox support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc9d04fd949a6f844cd4becf5fa591627471cbf6f479f4657a0bd7af570d5cc7</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:43:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election--3aadbd4431d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's largest Arab party grouping said Thursday it would recommend opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government, potentially bolstering his bid after Arab-majority lists won a record 19 seats in last week's election and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lost the support of an allied religious party.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi missiles fired at Medina intercepted, Saudi coalition says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1f41139b704871b8d36365e3d0aae7c0a29a46af5df4bd977915b39ecea2ba2</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:04:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:07:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-houthi-missiles-fired-at-medina-intercepted-saudi-coalition-says--19ce0f207758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-houthi-missiles-fired-at-medina-intercepted-saudi-coalition-says" /><summary type="html">A ballistic missile fired at the Saudi city of Medina, one of Islam's holiest cities, was intercepted Thursday, a spokesman for the Saudi-led coalition fighting Yemen's Houthi rebels said. The announcement came shortly after the kingdom's civil defence agency warned of potential danger around the strategic port of Yanbu.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu claims 'serious concerns' of foreign spending to sway Israeli election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cd2309667ee18517ca7a67146c32e740ad5ed62e348a6d7e3978f293b45db95</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election--38bacb102ad6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Wednesday cited "serious suspicions" around foreign interference in Israel's recent parliamentary elections. He claims foreign countries spent large amounts of money to influence the results, while the largest Arab-Israeli bloc called such accusations "political persecution".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Iran's deputy parliament speaker reacts to Trump's elections setback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a7aec2b60c9587f21615403a7bb9a3a549d1d9821bd89d659800d4b2c70d11d</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:50:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1--b3baa850b100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1" /><summary type="html">First Deputy Speaker of the Parliament of Iran Ali Nikzad on Wednesday attributed Republican losses in the US midterm elections to Washington's war with Iran, telling lawmakers that American efforts to pressure Tehran had failed.  Democrats won control of both chambers of Congress in Tuesday's midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>What consequences for Israel as Democrats win the US midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dd8f8043732b30d7251a1fb5ee8704c8cef83635568a8851a9fdb11648a9a7e</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:32:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-what-consequences-for-israel-as-democrats-win-the-us-midterm-elections--b88554bea6f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-what-consequences-for-israel-as-democrats-win-the-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Democrats seized control of the US Congress on Tuesday, capturing the Senate and House of Representatives in a stunning upset. What are the potential consequences for Israel and Benjamin Netanyahu, as Trump announced on Tuesday that the US will halt $3.8 billion in aid to the country? FRANCE 24's correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Four oil tankers destroyed in Hormuz after hitting mines, Tehran says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40d7e3db4f9b487ecac6caddba5a2493e44447f24d79e268118d9642a305efc9</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T08:43:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-four-oil-tankers-destroyed-in-hormuz-after-hitting-mines-tehran-says--117c71d9585d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-four-oil-tankers-destroyed-in-hormuz-after-hitting-mines-tehran-says" /><summary type="html">Four oil tankers caught fire after hitting mines in the Strait of Hormuz, Tehran claimed Wednesday, a day after US President Donald Trump said the United States had launched strikes on Iran. Discussions to end the war between Washington and Tehran via mediators have continued with little sign of diplomatic breakthrough.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's President Herzog accepts certified election results, urges compromise to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:193db8dcd05088f4a076c1c87aab29587142261d21e21533e8cd2b437bff61e3</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T02:05:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-israel-s-herzog-urges-compromise-to-form-government-after-divisive-election--72801d1bfaac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-israel-s-herzog-urges-compromise-to-form-government-after-divisive-election" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Wednesday formally accepted the certified results from last week’s legislative elections which delivered no clear winner, and said he would begin consultations regarding the formation of a new government. Both Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his main challenger, former military chief Gadi Eisenkot, are negotiating to form a governing coalition.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump cuts Israeli military aid: $3.8 billion in security assistance slashed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b42419d5ebc3369110677a1f950c7b5db04750234c1cc135494d19eee2726eee</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:01:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-trump-cuts-israeli-military-aid-3-8-billion-in-security-assistance-slashed--9e8be08da6ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-trump-cuts-israeli-military-aid-3-8-billion-in-security-assistance-slashed" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, November 3, said he made a deal with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu for Washington to stop providing $3.8 billion in funding to Israel after the end of this year. FRANCE 24's Jerusalem correspondent, Noga Tarnopolsky, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says US will halt $4 billion in aid to Israel at the end of the year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96b493b28dd0b6f4f41f8076e8ae9cedf25b2a2cd4eb32c497293e288e06c48b</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:35:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-trump-says-us-will-halt-4-billion-in-aid-to-israel-after-end-of-this-year--ad88efbaf029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-trump-says-us-will-halt-4-billion-in-aid-to-israel-after-end-of-this-year" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Tuesday said the United States will halt its $4 billion in annual funding to Israel at the end of the year. Speaking to Fox News, the US president added that Israel no longer needed the aid from Washington, and that some politicians were using the funding package to criticise Republicans.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US strikes Iran's Qeshm Island as midterm elections start</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ca4ff4c0bbfb110d19437bc9fc778143f8556f402e06325d5c08ba265308e65</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-strikes-iran-s-qeshm-island-as-midterm-elections-start--40705a7ad889.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-strikes-iran-s-qeshm-island-as-midterm-elections-start" /><summary type="html">The United States has conducted defensive strikes on some Iranian targets in the Strait of Hormuz, a US official said Monday, on the eve of crucial midterm elections. The unpopular Iran war and the resulting impact on U.S. gasoline prices and other parts of the economy have been a vulnerability for Republicans as they try to keep control of Congress. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Oliver Farry has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli opposition unites behind Eisenkot as Netanyahu says voters chose him for PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd2bb169e0253c25e84d095d04d7f4e6bd8f15a3abb58169d74d060ea358bf7d</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T09:03:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-israeli-opposition-unites-behind-eisenkot-netanyahu-voters-chose-him-pm--9824217a7593.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-israeli-opposition-unites-behind-eisenkot-netanyahu-voters-chose-him-pm" /><summary type="html">Israel's opposition is on Tuesday due to meet for the first time since last week's closely contested election in which neither Gadi Eisenkot's change bloc nor incumbent Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's right-wing alliance managed to win a majority in the Knesset. All parties in Eisenkot's camp have endorsed him to be the next prime minister, but the hot-button issue will be whether to unite with the Arab parties who made surprise gains in the vote.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US strikes Iran's Qeshm Island as Trump signals progress in talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a7a0be85a8755304b3b3b4c29c00befa1fb6265655da0e4f788ec6c04253844</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T02:28:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-us-strikes-iran-qeshm-island-as-trump-signals-progress-in-talks--78af20e4e6db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261103-us-strikes-iran-qeshm-island-as-trump-signals-progress-in-talks" /><summary type="html">The United States reportedly struck Iran's Qeshm Island on Monday, even as President Donald Trump signalled progress in negotiations with Tehran to end the eight-month-old conflict. The reported attack was the latest in a series of limited strikes Washington has secretly carried out in recent weeks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli 'unity government': Efrat Shapira expects Herzog will urge rival camps to form a 'coalition'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7330638869db1ed939f363d48f44455d95050caed7ef5e10bc782423cafd60e4</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T19:15:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-unity-government-efrat-shapira-expects-herzog-will-urge-rival-camps-to-form-a-coalition--6946ac5dfcf1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-unity-government-efrat-shapira-expects-herzog-will-urge-rival-camps-to-form-a-coalition" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Efrat Shapira Rosenberg, Israeli Radio/TV Host, Columnist, Podcaster and Educator. Following a deadlocked Israeli election, “everyone is saying who they’re not going to sit with, but no one is actually saying who they will sit with.” As President Isaac Herzog prepares to consult parliamentary factions over the formation of a new coalition, the impasse reveals tensions that extend beyond the familiar confrontation between Benjamin Netanyahu and his political opponents. According to Shapira, co-host of the highly popular Israeli politics podcast Miflaget Hamakshavot, the divisions are equally pronounced within the opposition bloc supporting Gadi Eisenkot.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says deal with Tehran 'could happen' amid 'intensive' talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4cf7745a64298155aadb8cf0f3078b2da667cecc338c07f2bfb5e6acb535250</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T17:42:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-iran-engages-us-in-intensive-negotiations-to-avert-fresh-war-outbreak--06664a4986cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-iran-engages-us-in-intensive-negotiations-to-avert-fresh-war-outbreak" /><summary type="html">Tehran on Monday said that the country was holding "intensive" indirect talks with Washington to avoid a fresh round of US attacks on Iran ahead of the US midterm elections this week. Foreign ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei shared Iranian plans to reopen blockaded energy corridor, the Strait of Hormuz, if the US were to meet its demands.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran offers deal on Hormuz Strait, Netanyahu wants to 'finish the job'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfc24fe5ef4ef1a79c8dee641692dd08e1c19fb2140c39c006f0a1f0a44711a9</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T17:04:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-iran-offers-deal-on-hormuz-strait-netanyahu-wants-to-finish-the-job--ec0e4b1d1cc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-iran-offers-deal-on-hormuz-strait-netanyahu-wants-to-finish-the-job" /><summary type="html">Iran said Monday it had a two-day plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and resume nuclear talks with the United States, shortening a process originally expected to take seven days. Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he wanted to "finish the job" first. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's president begins process of coalition government negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39a9d275d5809f489fa3987e9c77ccd4b6b70696c8f7a51b0e97f831207b15f9</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-israel-s-president-begins-process-of-coalition-government-negotiations--73c7e4dcefb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-israel-s-president-begins-process-of-coalition-government-negotiations" /><summary type="html">Israel's President Isaac Herzog begins the process of coalition government negotiations this week. One possibility is for the centrist opposition bloc to form a government with the Arab parties, which would oust current Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Protests for and against such a coalition this weekend made it clear the Israeli public is divided over the idea.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli army withdraws from Hebron after operation displaces thousands of Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f542c01c122cda447be93628a81a1dc17357f89f1ae0a4941c0d099d683a7814</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T09:51:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-israeli-army-withdraws-from-hebron-after-operation-displaces-thousands-of-palestinians--be564477bc3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-israeli-army-withdraws-from-hebron-after-operation-displaces-thousands-of-palestinians" /><summary type="html">Israeli forces withdrew from a neighbourhood in the occupied West Bank city of Hebron on Monday, ending a military operation launched after two Israeli soldiers were killed in late October. Thousands of Palestinians displaced during the raid have begun returning to homes, many of which were damaged or ransacked.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran warns renewed war with US could outlast previous conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17a0ce2636ceadb0b13a005a75d91300853c4de0d331c2e414302bb4f09e18a1</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T00:23:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-iran-warns-renewed-war-with-us-could-outlast-previous-conflict--c78a8619ee88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-iran-warns-renewed-war-with-us-could-outlast-previous-conflict" /><summary type="html">Iran on Sunday said that a renewed war with the United States could last longer than the previous round of fighting, as President Donald Trump suggested that Washington still had targets to strike. Tehran threatened retaliation without geographical limits while diplomatic efforts continued to avert a fresh escalation ahead of Tuesday's US midterm elections.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's Khamenei warns US and Israel against new attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2969ba8565ca513d844e4b8551aa4bfd658a8ca822aade36688f439fd165f01a</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T17:00:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261031-iran-s-khamenei-warns-us-and-israel-against-new-attacks--ffe715e07f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261031-iran-s-khamenei-warns-us-and-israel-against-new-attacks" /><summary type="html">Iran's supreme leader warned the United States and Israel on Saturday against further strikes as tensions mount over a possible return to fighting. US President Donald Trump and Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu have threatened new military action on Tehran but US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Trump had not yet made a decision on fresh strikes.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: 'Netanyahu did not win, he lost dramatically,' former PM Barak says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5963a0dfceda69062468271b580c490e056b037c7d68c2dc61e5a429a19baae0</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T15:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261030-israeli-election-netanyahu-did-not-win-he-lost-dramatically-former-pm-barak-says--bd0fe6fcb613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261030-israeli-election-netanyahu-did-not-win-he-lost-dramatically-former-pm-barak-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, former Israeli prime minister Ehud Barak said Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu "did not win" this week's election in Israel but "lost dramatically", and that his rival Gadi Eisenkot should ally with Arab parties. Barak also suggested that claims of Qatari funding for an Arab party aimed to distract from an ongoing corruption scandal, and warned that Netanyahu was ready to strike Iran to stay in power.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's election ends in deadlock as final results show no clear winner</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61f5aba575de820e5326906ce9e49c9a384257d4d9445541aa0cf11ae10dc233</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T15:24:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-israel-s-election-ends-in-deadlock-as-final-results-show-no-clear-winner--404f62861054.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-israel-s-election-ends-in-deadlock-as-final-results-show-no-clear-winner" /><summary type="html">Israel's wartime election appeared deadlocked on Tuesday, exit polls showed, ​with Gadi Eisenkot's opposition bloc running neck and neck with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's camp, leaving neither side with a clear path to power. The projections pointed to a setback for Netanyahu's coalition and potentially weeks of political wrangling to form a government. FRANCE 24's Jerusalem correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu bloc leads but lacks majority, Israel's official results show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4556655fbbcf470bcb6ab4570e5600f6835065b1f6c6cc0db42165198ba482cf</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T02:29:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261030-netanyahu-bloc-in-lead-without-majority-in-israel-election-say-official-results--2dc8a1ab3b52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261030-netanyahu-bloc-in-lead-without-majority-in-israel-election-say-official-results" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's coalition won the most seats in the general election but fell eight short of a parliamentary majority, final results showed Friday. Arab party groupings emerged as potential kingmakers, while allegations of foreign interference threatened to complicate efforts to form a government.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israelis await final election results as difficult choices lie ahead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9140d94e3f4f095c59e2ee362fe5743470be037c35fc7c987404d04603ac950</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:59:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-israelis-await-final-election-results-as-difficult-choices-lie-ahead--611940c40736.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-israelis-await-final-election-results-as-difficult-choices-lie-ahead" /><summary type="html">Israelis awaited the final election results on Thursday to confirm what appeared to be taking shape: neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his allies nor the array of parties seeking to oust him seemed likely to secure a majority of seats in parliament. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu piles pressure on Arab parties with claims of foreign funding to 'steal' election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2826580c990f2b4dca2c1572d344c3621beeacd0ae3eb647fd9dfd5e79e13836</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T09:46:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261029-netanyahu-piles-pressure-on-arab-parties-with-claims-of-foreign-funding-to-steal-election--069320dc4748.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261029-netanyahu-piles-pressure-on-arab-parties-with-claims-of-foreign-funding-to-steal-election" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his party Likud on Thursday sought to amplify unproven claims that Arab parties had received foregn funding ahead of the country's national elections as Netanyahu's opponents accused him of seeking to "delegitimise" the results of the vote.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel finishes vote count, Netanyahu's Likud biggest party but without majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:189dca292542528412d33e13f72cca96947934a803334ea53a8b734d856b8a96</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T03:36:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261029-live-israeli-elections-are-coming-to-a-close-with-no-majority-to-be-seen--43db87e7143d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261029-live-israeli-elections-are-coming-to-a-close-with-no-majority-to-be-seen" /><summary type="html">Israel on Thursday completed its vote count from the country's national elections with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's bloc securing 53 seats (27 of which went to his party Likud) and other parties securing 67 seats in the Knesset. With no party gaining an outright majority, weeks of jockeying to form a government are set to follow. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Historic gains for Arab-majority parties in Israeli election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b889c621bbf0a7d0861654584d9b1b8b19dfc8cc97f9831e3b064dd9f94ab8f0</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T20:32:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/historic-gains-for-arab-majority-parties-in-israeli-election--ef69df2f3ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/historic-gains-for-arab-majority-parties-in-israeli-election" /><summary type="html">Two Arab-majority parties are set to win a historic 19 seats in total, amid a record turnout at the polls in Israel on Tuesday. Voters from the community, descendants of Palestinians who stayed after Israel's creation and who make up around 20 percent of the population, have been enraged by the Netanyahu government's ultra-nationalist Jewish vision for the country and the Palestinian territories. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Which way will Israel break? Netanyahu still in it after election night surprises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c27ae7a4ac03e6f9387d4b696d66793cacde9a53e3b93fd64a975964fa62559</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:34:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261028-which-way-will-israel-break-netanyahu-still-in-it-after-election-night-surprises--5418ddd2326d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261028-which-way-will-israel-break-netanyahu-still-in-it-after-election-night-surprises" /><summary type="html">In Israel, the surprises only start with election night. They're still counting ballots in a vote that featured the highest turnout in decades, historic inroads by Arab parties and Benjamin Netanyahu's worst result since 1999. And yet, Israel's longest-serving prime minister still has a path to staying in power. As we await the definitive makeup of the next parliament, our panel breaks out the calculators and pie charts: in what scenario does Netanyahu survive? Is the issue with the right-wing Likud leader or his policies?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'Israeli electorate has moved rightward: Many underestimated extent of fracture in Israeli society'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb2e1422a763c735adf30eee48f0a5ab27917db4b07a5e9ffc684ab2126388c1</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:12:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-electorate-has-moved-rightward-many-underestimated-extent-of-fracture-in-israeli-society--c43137dced55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-electorate-has-moved-rightward-many-underestimated-extent-of-fracture-in-israeli-society" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Dr. Shira Efron, RAND's Distinguished Israel Policy Chair. “Many of us, myself included, underestimated the extent of the fracture in Israeli society.” It reflects a political system in which ideological polarisation, the rightward shift of the Jewish electorate and the contested legitimacy of Arab political participation have sharply narrowed the possibilities for coalition-building. Dr. Efron illustrates a political landscape in which Netanyahu’s governing bloc has lost ground, yet still has “more cards, or better cards, to play,” she argues, whether through another election, a national unity government or attempts to draw opposition partners into his orbit.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel election: What impact on Iran as the war in the Middle East continues?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da97f90a91f5d73d86bd5fbe4b89bda1fd3982b97e035ef79aca7bb9056cc11f</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:54:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israel-election-what-impact-on-iran-as-the-war-in-the-middle-east-continues--3eb40a582df2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israel-election-what-impact-on-iran-as-the-war-in-the-middle-east-continues" /><summary type="html">Benjamin Netanyahu is expected to face greater constraints as Israel’s caretaker prime minister following Tuesday’s election. However, experts say his government could retain significant powers, including the authority to wage war against Iran. So what impact will the election have on Israel’s approach to Iran? France 24’s International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Arab parties ‘have woken up’: Israel's uncertain election may deliver surprise kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:157bdc866ee39202db9ab956162f77a254402c97340c15d3267c23fd45537023</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:04:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261028-arab-parties-have-woken-up-israel-uncertain-election-may-deliver-surprise-kingmakers--f902aaf3d82e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261028-arab-parties-have-woken-up-israel-uncertain-election-may-deliver-surprise-kingmakers" /><summary type="html">Uncertainty hung over Israel’s election Wednesday as neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s right-wing, religious bloc nor the bloc formed by his centrist rival Gadi Eisenkot appeared to be heading for a majority in the Knesset. But there was a surprise: an unusually strong showing by Arab parties could make them unexpected kingmakers.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
